{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegralSummability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegralSummability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Module","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.resummation_sub_ak_mem_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.resummation_sub_ak_mem_span","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L189-L196","doc":"**The resummation differs from the AK integral by a `ℤ[q^±]`-combination\nof state integrals.** Both `resummation d` and `I_{0,0}` lie in the\nspan (FW combination relation + `ak_integral_mem_span`), and the span\nis a submodule, so their difference does too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.ak_integral_mem_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.ak_integral_mem_span","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L182-L187","doc":"**The Andersen–Kashaev integral lies in the state-integral module.**\nThe AK integral is the `(m,ℓ) = (0,0)` state integral, so it is a\ngenerator of the span. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.frame_transport_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.frame_transport_trans","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L157-L180","doc":"**Path-independence of Borel–Laplace resummation.** Transporting the\nframe from `a` to `c` directly equals transporting `a → b → c`: for\nevery component `i`,\n`frame c i = ∑ⱼ (S_{a,c})ⱼᵢ • frame a j`.\nDerived by composing the `frame_transport` field with the\n`stokes_cocycle` field — the genuine work of the cocycle on the\nstate-integral data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_mul_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_mul_symm","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L151-L155","doc":"**Two-sided composition of a Stokes matrix with its reverse is the\nidentity:** `S_{ϑ₁,ϑ₂} · S_{ϑ₂,ϑ₁} = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_inv","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L144-L149","doc":"**Reverse direction = inverse Stokes matrix:** `(S_{ϑ₁,ϑ₂})⁻¹ =\nS_{ϑ₂,ϑ₁}`. Derived from the cocycle and `stokes_refl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_refl","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L136-L142","doc":"**No Stokes jump along a single ray:** `S_{ϑ,ϑ} = 1`.\nDerived from the cocycle — `S_{ϑ,ϑ}` is idempotent in the group\n`GL (Fin rank) R`, hence the identity. This is *not* a field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_cocycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes_cocycle","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L128-L128","doc":"**FW Stokes cocycle (eq. 27, groupoid form).**\n`S_{ϑ₁,ϑ₂} · S_{ϑ₂,ϑ₃} = S_{ϑ₁,ϑ₃}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.frame_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.frame_transport","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L121-L121","doc":"**FW transport (eq. 26).** Changing the resummation direction acts\non the frame by right-multiplication by the Stokes matrix:\n`Î_{j,ϑ₂} = Î_{j,ϑ₁} · S_{ϑ₁,ϑ₂}`, i.e. componentwise\n`frame b i = ∑ⱼ (S_{a,b})ⱼᵢ • frame a j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stokes","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L116-L116","doc":"The Stokes matrices `S_{ϑ₁,ϑ₂}(q) ∈ GL_{max{A,B}}(ℤ[q^±])`\n(FW eq. 26). Valued in the general linear group over `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.frame","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.frame","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L113-L113","doc":"The frame `Î_{j,ϑ}`: the `r`-tuple of independent resummed series\ncollected in FW eq. (25), as a map `D → (Fin rank → M)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.resummation_mem_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.resummation_mem_span","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L109-L109","doc":"**FW combination relation.** Away from Stokes rays the resummation\nis a `ℤ[q^±]`-linear combination of state integrals: it lies in the\n`R`-span of the `I_{m,ℓ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.resummation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.resummation","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L105-L105","doc":"The Borel–Laplace resummation of `Φ_Ξ` in admissible direction `ϑ`;\na single distinguished element of the state-integral module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stateIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.stateIntegral","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The Andersen–Kashaev state integrals `I_{m,ℓ} ∈ M`, indexed by\n`(m, ℓ) ∈ ℤ × ℤ`. The `(0,0)` member is the AK integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.rank","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The rank `r = max{A,B}` — the number of critical points / the size\nof the Stokes matrices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelStateIntegral.BorelSummableToStateIntegral","kind":"class","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelStateIntegralSummability.lean#L71-L129","doc":"**Hypotheses / inputs of Fantini–Wheeler Theorem 1.4**\n([fantini-wheeler2024], arXiv:2410.20973), axiomatized as a Lean\nclass over a generic base ring `R` (standing for `ℤ[q^±]`).\n\nType parameters:\n* `R` — the base ring (`ℤ[q^±]`).\n* `M` — the `R`-module spanned by the state integrals `I_{m,ℓ}`.\n* `D` — the admissible resummation directions `ϑ` (args avoiding\n  Stokes rays); left abstract.\n\nThe rank `r = max{A,B}` is the number of critical points (FW: \"there\nare `max{A,B}` critical points\"). The fields carry the *inputs* FW\nproves exist; the downstream theorems derive consequences.\n\nThe cocycle field is stated in groupoid-completed form (all triples),\nthe standard resurgent-structure encoding of FW eq. (27), which holds\nfor ordered `ϑ₁ < ϑ₂ < ϑ₃` and extends by `S_{ϑ,ϑ} := 1`,\n`S_{ϑ',ϑ} := S_{ϑ,ϑ'}⁻¹`.\n\n§3b-cond non-degeneracy: no field carries a downstream theorem's own\nconclusion. `stokes_refl` / `stokes_inv` are *derived* from\n`stokes_cocycle` via the group structure of `GL (Fin rank) R`;\n`frame_transport_trans` is *derived* from `frame_transport` + the\ncocycle. ","signatureChunk":0}]}